From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 13:56:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(glm cuda): --parallel N on two ranks: one cache pool,
 batched verify rounds (each reply its solo bits)

--parallel N (2 to 4, the same on both ranks) decodes up to N GLM-5.3-Flash requests together; each reply is the one
its request gets alone with "draft": false. Without --parallel nothing changes.

- One cache pool (pool.py, forward.Caches): every per-token cache (DSA latents, the indexer's keys, gates and pooled
  keys, the MTP layer's) is one pool of rows, the window's slots plus what TF_GLM_CACHE_GIB gives kept prompts, cut
  into 2,048-token extents; a stream or kept prompt owns one and grows up to the window. forward.Slots holds each
  stream's KDA states, conv windows and window scratch; forward.State views an extent and a slot (without a pool it
  makes its own, as before). A request the pool cannot place waits; when every decoding stream waits for room the
  youngest goes back to the queue and replays (its sent tokens owed, not sent again).
- Batched verify rounds (verify.BatchedVerify): every decoding stream's window (pending token and drafts, 32 rows
  in all) in one forward: the row-independent work on all rows, the KDA and DSA layers through the segmented kernels
  (forward.kda_segments / dsa_segments as the layers' mixer); one CUDA graph a window size.
  TF_GLM_MULTI_VERIFY=serial verifies each window as its own forward (verify.SerialVerify, the reference).
- Drafts: DFlash2 streams in one batched block pass and context update a round (dflash2_multi); MTP streams on the
  MTP head from their own cache rows (the head's graphs at home, eager elsewhere). auto drafts with DFlash2 when it
  is loaded, else with the single-stream auto's MTP rule; MTP and DFlash2 policies fall back to their twins.
  Under --parallel an unset TF_GLM_MTP means auto: beside DFlash2 the MTP head is not loaded (about 2 GiB a rank);
  TF_GLM_MTP=1 loads it, and without DFlash2 it loads as before (engine.mtp_head's ``parallel``).
- Prompts fill in chunks between rounds (decode.prefill_chunk on the stream's state): TF_GLM_FILL_ROWS (1,024) rows
  while others decode, the engine's chunk otherwise, TF_GLM_FILL_SHARE (0.5) of the iterations. A drafted prompt is
  kept before its last token, as the single-stream prefill keeps it: the same prompt again or the next turn resumes
  there, in place or copied, with its DFlash2 window or MTP rows.
- Two ranks (multi.MultiDecoder, multi.GlmScheduler): rank 0 decides admissions, placement and rounds and sends one
  message an iteration (ADMIT, EVICT, MOVE, GROW, FILL, ROUND, SLOT, FINISH, IDLE); rank 1 applies it, derives the
  drafts itself and checks the depths; an idle rank 1 waits on the doorbell. A client that leaves ends its stream at
  the next round boundary on both ranks. /health adds the decoder's counts (paused streams, the pool's free tokens,
  kept prompts). /v1/decisions keeps --parallel 1.
- Speed settings that never change a reply (multi_tune.py): TF_GLM_MULTI_SAMPLER=packed, TF_GLM_MULTI_DEPTH=joint /
  scale:A, TF_GLM_MULTI_ASYNC=1, TF_GLM_MULTI_LONE=1 (a lone stream on the one-stream graphs; off by default),
  TF_GLM_MULTI_PROFILE=N; TF_GLM_MULTI_WATCHDOG_S dumps stacks of a stalled iteration.

Hooks in the existing code: GlmEngine(parallel=) and the cuda_engine option; the memory estimate (extra slots, the
batched selection's scores, the multi-stream drafter's rings, the pool from TF_GLM_CACHE_GIB); the two-rank settings
comparison; generate(background=) through the scheduler; follow() through the decoder; decode.Engine's
streams / pool_rows, use(st) and graphed(st) (only a state at the graphs' home replays them); compute's mixer;
health.py merges a decoder's own counts.

Tests: tests/test_glm_multi.py (CPU, two ranks through recorded messages on a fake model whose logits hash what its
stream committed from its pool rows and slot: staggered DFlash2, MTP, mixed and serial requests at 2 and 4 streams,
cancellation, pause and give-back, moves and evictions, resumes in place and copied, one message an iteration, every
speed setting, the threaded scheduler, /health, the packed sampler; each reply against the single-stream
GlmEngine.generate(draft=False), both ranks' state compared after every iteration), tests/test_glm_pool.py and
tests/test_glm_mtp_setting.py (the --parallel MTP default) (CPU);
tests/cuda/test_glm_multi.py (GPU, the synthetic checkpoint with DFlash2 and the MTP head: concurrent requests
against a --parallel 1 engine's serial replies, resumed turns, cancellation, moved extents, batched windows against
serial ones, grammars, a mirror rank, the lone-stream graphs, every speed setting, both ranks' startup collectives,
two ranks with real all-gathers). docs/recipes/glm-5.3-flash.md and the README describe it.

From the GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 2x DGX Sparks recipe (MiaAI-Lab), patches 0030, 0035, 0040 (its engine part), 0041 and
0048, without the recipe's speed-only changes (copy drafts, prompt grid, noise policies, hyper-connection split, FP8
KV, the RoCE transport, tuned defaults); MTP streams are new here.

